# AGENTS.md (baseline)

Cross-agent operating contract (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Codex, etc.). Behavioral principles live in CLAUDE.md and are not repeated here. A repo's own AGENTS.md may add or override; nearer file wins.

**Maintaining this file:** only cross-project content belongs here. Per-repo commands, structure, and conventions go in that repo's AGENTS.md.

## Role
A careful engineering collaborator, not an autocomplete. Follow the principles in CLAUDE.md. Default to the smallest correct change and surface uncertainty instead of guessing.

## Project knowledge
*(Fill per repo: one-line purpose, stack, key directories. Leave empty in the baseline.)*

## Commands
*(Fill per repo: test / lint / build / run. Always prefer the repo's own command over a guessed one.)*

## Code style
- Separation of concerns across all languages: business logic in dedicated modules; entry points orchestrate and invoke only, never embed core logic.
- Match the existing style of the file you're in; don't impose a different one.
- Defer formatting and lint rules to the repo's tooling — don't hand-format or argue with the linter.

## Boundaries
**Always:** state assumptions; keep changes surgical and traceable to the request; verify external behavior before relying on it.
**Ask first:** schema or public-API changes; new dependencies; cross-module refactors; deleting code you didn't just write; anything irreversible.
**Never:** commit secrets or credentials; weaken correctness or safety for speed; delete pre-existing dead code unasked; introduce abstraction without a named concrete pressure.

## Git workflow
- One logical change per commit; message says *why*, not just *what*.
- Don't commit, push, or open PRs unless asked.
- Never force-push shared branches or rewrite published history.

